#: ../folio-assistant-core/collab/processes/content/editing-hci-validation.bpmn:227
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "On the edge out of `Task_ReviewFindings` and before `Task_RecordDecision`: the findings are the evidence, so the options can only be weighed once they exist, and after `Task_RecordDecision` the decision is already written down. Not between `Gateway_EditorDecision` and `Task_RecordDecision`: `Flow_21b` runs `Task_RecordDecision` -> `Gateway_EditorDecision`, so the gateway reads a decision already recorded. In the Agent lane: the subprocess records that the options were WEIGHED (its own `decision-audit` note), and `Task_RecordDecision` in `Lane_Editor` records WHAT WAS CHOSEN. The analyst is not the decider. (`CallActivity_Evidence` is in `Lane_Editor` because the author performs the retrieval.) On the trigger: `A_Frame` opens the subprocess on `opening-brief`'s trigger — irreversibility and surprise — and leaving there is a correct outcome. A spelling fix that reached `Task_ReviewFindings` with one mechanical finding exits immediately; a revise-or-discard on a block other content depends on does not."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/collab/processes/content/editing-hci-validation.bpmn:267
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Only now does the change become corpus content, together with its QA sidecars. Subject to the commit-hygiene requirement."
msgstr ""

